  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has recently started learning from the new CodeChef SQL course.\n\nHe has a table which initially has RRR rows and CCC columns. He then adds EEE extra rows to it. How many total cells does he have finally?\n\n\nInput Format\nThe only line in the input contains three space-separated integers RRR, CCC, and EEE — the number of initial rows, the number of columns, and the number of extra rows added, respectively.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput on a new line, a single integer, which should be the final total number of cells in the table.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤R≤1001 \\leq R \\leq 1001≤R≤100",
      "1≤C≤1001 \\leq C \\leq 1001≤C≤100",
      "1≤E≤1001 \\leq E \\leq 1001≤E≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5 2 1",
        "output": "12",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are initially 555 rows, and 222 columns. So the initial number of cells was 5∗2=105 * 2 = 105∗2=10.\nThen, 111 extra row was added. So now the table has 666 rows, and 222 columns. So the total number of cells is now 6∗2=126 * 2 = 126∗2=12, which is the answer."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "6 10 3",
        "output": "90",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are initially 666 rows, and 101010 columns. So the initial number of cells was 6∗10=606 * 10 = 606∗10=60.\nThen, 333 extra rows were added. So now the table has 999 rows, and 101010 columns. So the total number of cells is now 9∗10=909 * 10 = 909∗10=90, which is the answer."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1 1 1",
        "output": "2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are initially 111 rows, and 111 columns. So the initial number of cells was 1∗1=11 * 1 = 11∗1=1.\nThen, 111 extra row was added. So now the table has 222 rows, and 111 columns. So the total number of cells is now 2∗1=22 * 1 = 22∗1=2, which is the answer."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_4",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "100 100 100",
        "output": "20000",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are initially 100100100 rows, and 100100100 columns. So the initial number of cells was 100∗100=10000100 * 100 = 10000100∗100=10000.\nThen, 100100100 extra rows were added. So now the table has 200200200 rows, and 100100100 columns. So the total number of cells is now 200∗100=20000200 * 100 = 20000200∗100=20000, which is the answer."
      }
    ]
  },
